TOTK: a guarded Ampere warp-collective instruction (VOTE, VOTEU, SHFL, MATCH, REDUX) runs in every active lane and its guard
only masks its register writes, as on the hardware. EmitOpsAmpere wrapped every guarded instruction in a branch, so a guarded
vote counted the lanes whose guard held and nothing else. The NVN2 compiler's warp-aggregated atomics take a VOTEU under the
leader lane's guard to count the lanes the leader adds for (VOTEU, POPC, ATOM.ADD): OoT's foliage culling kernel
(fe89d4116c26fddf) added one instance per warp, the other lanes wrote their instances over the next warps' slots, and the
mesh draws' counts and instance lists changed every frame with the camera still (trees, bushes and grass flickered and
vanished). Maxwell jobs are unchanged.

